  introductionManager: {fileID: 342094969}
  moleculeManager: {fileID: 846564644}
  sorbentManager: {fileID: 1155216670}
  hydroswingManager: {fileID: 2132780889}
  temperatureswingManager: {fileID: 164432794}
  electroswingManager: {fileID: 1730269768}
  captureManager: {fileID: 1541036193}
  airOutManager: {fileID: 1472239431}
  boxTop: {fileID: 1782861303}
  boxFront: {fileID: 761889134}
  airInUi: {fileID: 1023954003}
  levelTitleContainer: {fileID: 2062289903}
  levelDescriptionContainer: {fileID: 1019676950}
  interactiveDescriptionContainer: {fileID: 552594300}
  waitButton: {fileID: 984547212}
  nextButton: {fileID: 49245503}
  restartButton: {fileID: 954336376}
  releaseOptions: {fileID: 1536126709}
  toggleInstructions: {fileID: 74993774}
  levelTitle: {fileID: 1682646983}
  levelDescription: {fileID: 2127047845}
  interactiveTitle: {fileID: 1583056045}
  interactiveDescription: {fileID: 1225811356}
  airInSetUpTitle: Intake
  airInSetUpDescription: "Ambient air \u2014 currently laden with record shattering
    levels of the climate altering gas carbon dioxide \u2060\u2014 flows into the
    Direct Air Carbon Capture machine.\n\nHover over molecules to learn more abount
    them."
  airInTitle: Intake
  airInDescription: 'The machine will not work if it does not have any way to intake
    ambient air.


    Move your MOUSE and hold down LEFT MOUSE BUTTON to guide the
    molecules into the machine.'
  airInWaitText: 
  absorbSetUpTitle: CO2 Absorption
  absorbSetUpDescription: Once CO2 enters the machine, it will be absorbed by sorbent
    panel. When these panels are full, the carbon must then be released from them.
    There are three known ways to release carbon from a sorbent.
  absorbSetUpWaitText: 
  absorbTitles:
  - HYDRO
  - TEMPERATURE
  - ELECTRO
  absorbDescriptions:
  - 'Using the hydro-swing method, the sorbent will absorb CO2 when dry and release
    it when wet. '
  - Using the temperature-swing method, the sorbent will absorb CO2 and release it
    when heated.
  - Using the electro-swing method, the sorbent will absorb CO2 and release it when
    electrified.
  releaseTitle: Hydro-Swing
  releaseDescription: 'Now that the sorbent is full, the CO2 must be released and
    stored. This method uses a sorbent that releases absorbed CO2 when wet.


    Use
    your MOUSE to move the spout and LEFT CLICK to release water.'
  tempTitle: Temperature-Swing
  tempDescription: 'In order to prevent additional pollution related to generating
    heat, waste heat from factories is redirected.


    Use your mouse to turn the
    pipes and redirect waste heat to the carbon capture machine.'
  captureTitle: Collection
  captureDescription: 'Now that the carbon has been releasedfrom the sorbent it gathers
    in a tray to be collected for alternative use.


    Use your MOUSE to guide
    the vacuum, and hold down the LEFT MOUSE BUTTON to collect the carbon.'
  airOutTitle: Clean Air
  airOutDescription: Now that CO2 has been absorbed and stored, the Direct Air Carbon
    Capture machine will release clean air into the atmosphere. Notice that there
    clear air contains much less CO2 than previously.
  currentState: 0
